{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd && git status --short && rg --files | rg '(\"'^AGENTS.md$|10-filing-phase|CURRENT_STATE|codex-r70|PAID-GATE|paid_gate.py|reader-brief-v13|assemble_readings|judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-wdPfdfa1' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-23 02:11:38.783 xcodebuild[63677:74881562]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-23 02:11:38.955 xcodebuild[63677:74881560] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-aEsh9wqm' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-23 02:11:39.331 xcodebuild[63679:74881589]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-23 02:11:39.447 xcodebuild[63679:74881587] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n M docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n M docs/DECISIONS-log.md\n M docs/DECISIONS.md\n?? docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/\nAGENTS.md\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md\ndocs/archive/2026-10-22-v15/CURRENT_STATE.md\ndocs/archive/2026-10-16-v1/CURRENT_STATE.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r70.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r70.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/assemble_readings.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/reader-brief-v13.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/reader-brief-v13s.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r70b.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r70b.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba codex-r70.md && nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | tail -140 && nl -ba reader-brief-v13s.md && diff -u reader-brief-v13.md reader-brief-v13s.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba codex-r70.md && nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | tail -140 && nl -ba reader-brief-v13s.md && diff -u reader-brief-v13.md reader-brief-v13s.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Send with listed changes.** The 36 authorized requests are ready. Fix what the readers will see and correct the launch path before spending the one-time authorization. On a stored answer, the paid packet changes `F13` from $745B of capital expenditure to $750B of data-center spending while the explanation still points to `F13`. That can change a reader’s vote. [Stored answer:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/S/answers/claude.json:1) · [paid_gate.py:481](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:481)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Minor — the plan, authorization and spending checks pass.** I rebuilt all 12 requests from the archives in memory. The bytes match the `0dc7c310…` pin, and all 12 carry the registered `080a0012…` D751 system text. The three revenue snapshots have 237, 237 and 260 passages respectively, identical across the joint and separate calls for each snapshot. O, S and E have 35, 31 and 15. Three draws give 9 joint calls, 18 separate calls and 9 singletons. Against the saved pre-D753 control, the only changes in `paid_gate.py` are the new pin and authorization selection. I independently exercised the wrong ceiling, altered plan, mixed format, spent v13 authorization and repeat v13s launch with file operations mocked. All five were refused. The real v13 authorization exists, and the v13s authorization and output folder were absent at review time. [Registered cases:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:11) · [Plan pin:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.sha256:1) · [D751 pin:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind7.py:16) · [Case construction:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:142) · [Authorization checks:431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:431)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Serious — the paid packets can omit evidence or change what a figure reference means.** I passed all six real D751 writer answers through the paid card renderer. Three showed a defect. Both E cards lost passages they named. The accepted “can’t tell yet” answer lost six, including five the writer said weighed against the forecast. The S answer in the example above had seven figure references with no displayed figure and two pointing to a different figure. The renderer selects figures by following the outcome and market reference, renumbers them, and copies the explanation without updating its references. An unresolved answer has no outcome figure to follow. Section 4 promises readers the passages the answer names. The smallest repair is to include the passages and figures named by each card and make every displayed reference resolve to the figure the writer meant. Replay these six answers at $0 and check the IDs and values before launch. [Packet contract:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:254) · [Figure selection:519](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:519) · [Passage selection:531](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:531) · [E answer:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json:82)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Wording — put Alex’s two clarifications in the frozen v13s reader text before launch.** Keep §4’s four questions, thresholds and third-reader rule. For `usable`, a related figure can support a forecast when the answer explains why it fits the companies, period and quantity, and why its assumptions favor the chosen band. For a reaffirmed target near a boundary, “can’t tell yet” is usable when the answer weighs the evidence, gives the target as context and names the fact that would decide. A published number resting on an unsized adjustment that determines its band gets `deciding_gap=yes`. This distinction matters because `usable=no` alone on a singleton cannot trigger STOP. Give both readers and the adjudicator the same wording, without naming the E case or importing the free test’s voting procedure. [D747:11582](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11582) · [D753:11768](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11768) · [Registered questions:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:263) · [Verdict calculation:782](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:782)\n     8\t\n     9\t4. **Serious — use the exact frozen packet file for the reading.** The existing batching helper drops everything before `## P01`, including the key-commitment line. Its assembler later hashes the original file, so the verdict can accept that hash even though the readers received different text. The smallest course is to give every reader the exact `packets.md`, with assigned packet IDs separately. A third reader also gets the two readings on each disputed question. Check all 27 packets, 45 cards and required tie-breaks before invoking the one-shot `verdict`. [Exact-file rule:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:261) · [Batch slicing:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/assemble_readings.py:19) · [Hash assembly:71](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/assemble_readings.py:71) · [One-shot seal:719](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:719)\n    10\t\n    11\t5. **Minor — correct the launch path and distinguish the two kinds of retry.** From the repository root, the script is `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py`. Keep the detached log and PID outside the new output folder because `send()` refuses an existing folder. All 36 scored attempts precede any diagnostic retry. Each refused answer can receive one diagnostic retry. A network failure can separately cause up to three transport attempts within a scored call, each reserved against the same $0.50. A terminal transport failure on a first attempt makes the result INCOMPLETE. A failed diagnostic retry leaves a complete set of first attempts scoreable. The stub cannot establish live provider availability, and the authorization is consumed before the first connection. Perform the registered machine and network check before launch. [Proposed command:22](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round70-brief.md:22) · [Launch guard:434](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:434) · [Retry order:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:232) · [Transport reservations:272](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:272) · [Completeness:219](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:219) · [Launch procedure:429](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:429)\n    12\t\n    13\t**Verdict — send with those changes under D753.** Both the stored $37B E forecast and the justified “can’t tell yet” pass the paid E schema and code checks. Readers rejected the former and accepted the latter. That is why faithful packets matter. Only the paid comparison can establish how Luna answers and whether judging the pair together helps. A pass earns production design work only. This review changed no files, sent no requests and spent $0. [Blind results:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:10) · [Decision authorized:11763](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11763)   178\t\n   179\t- **The record:** an attempt that was started and not finished is kept in `results.json` as interrupted.\n   180\t- **Rehearsal:** 51 of 51, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   181\t  - the scoring text has no attempt, decision or code;\n   182\t  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n   183\t  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n   184\t  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n   185\t  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n   186\t  - an interrupted card says the request was started.\n   187\t- **Mutants:** 20 of 20 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   188\t\n   189\t## 3f. After council round 47e (`codex-r47e.md`)\n   190\t\n   191\t- **[47e.1] The first attempt is scored, on both arms.**\n   192\t  - In the joint arm, a cross-card conflict (C3) is refused and retried with its reason, so the retry can repair it. In the separate\n   193\t    arm, the same conflict appears only when the two answers are reconciled, after both calls are over, and there is no retry.\n   194\t  - Scoring the final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have.\n   195\t  - D725 registered both arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about retries. Its pass and stop lines stay as\n   196\t    written and are applied to the first attempts.\n   197\t  - Retries are still sent and read for diagnosis (`attempts.md`), and are not counted.\n   198\t  - Rehearsed: the joint pair is published after its retry, but its refused first attempt is scored, so both arms come out at 6.\n   199\t- **[47e.2] One unit.** A shared forecast is unified only when the two copies have the same unit, as well as the same value and bounds.\n   200\t  Rehearsed: 110 USD bn against 110 USD is refused (C4).\n   201\t- **[47e.3] Every returned text is readable.**\n   202\t  - When the format check fails an answer, the scoring packet keeps its neutral label.\n   203\t  - The text the model returned, and the passages it names, go to `attempts.md` under a blind label. This covers both a first attempt\n   204\t    and a final one that fails the format.\n   205\t- **[47e.4] One verdict per run.**\n   206\t  - `verdict` copies the readings into the run once (`readings.json`, created exclusively).\n   207\t  - It scores them and writes `verdict.json` once, holding the readings' sha256, the key commitment, the packets' sha256, the run digest\n   208\t    and the result.\n   209\t  - A second verdict on the run is refused. `paid_gate.py replay` recomputes from the sealed readings and must reproduce the result.\n   210\t  - Rehearsed: the second verdict is refused; replay reproduces the result; after the sealed readings are edited, replay fails.\n   211\t- **Rehearsal:** 55 of 55, run three times (`rehearsal.log`).\n   212\t- **Mutants:** 25 of 25 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   213\t  - Two obsolete mutants were repointed or removed.\n   214\t  - One mutant crashed on a missing file and not on the defence. The test was corrected, and the mutant now fails the right check.\n   215\t\n   216\t## 3g. After council round 47f (`codex-r47f.md`)\n   217\t\n   218\t- **[47f.1] Retries cannot decide whether the scored test is complete.**\n   219\t  - The run sends every first attempt (all 36) before any retry.\n   220\t  - Completeness is judged on the first attempts: each must end published, held or refused.\n   221\t  - A retry that fails in transport, is interrupted or is never sent stays in the diagnostic record.\n   222\t  - Rehearsed: an interruption during a retry leaves all 36 scored attempts and a complete verdict. A transport failure on a retry\n   223\t    leaves the verdict complete. An interruption during a scored attempt makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. In the journal, every first\n   224\t    attempt comes before every retry.\n   225\t- **[47f.2] Every returned text survives.**\n   226\t  - The record keeps the provider's whole response, as the archive stores it, with no 20,000-character cut.\n   227\t  - A null content is shown as the model's refusal, or as \"no text returned\".\n   228\t  - Both files are rendered before anything is written, and a failed render leaves no files.\n   229\t  - Rehearsed: a refusal with null content, a 25,000-character malformed answer whose passage is named at its end, and a render that\n   230\t    fails and then succeeds.\n   231\t- **Rehearsal:** 61 of 61, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   232\t- **Mutants:** 30 of 30 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`). Two mutants are caught by the crash the defence prevents:\n   233\t  - without the interrupted branch, the summary fails on an unfinished attempt;\n   234\t  - passing a null content on, packet rendering fails.\n   235\t\n   236\t## 3h. After council round 47g (`codex-r47g.md`)\n   237\t\n   238\t- **[47g] Two journals, read on the writer's own delimiter.**\n   239\t  - Scored first attempts are written to `answers.jsonl`, and diagnostic retries to `retries.jsonl`. The run digest covers both.\n   240\t  - A damaged line in `answers.jsonl` makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. A damaged line in `retries.jsonl` is reported and marks that retry\n   241\t    interrupted, but leaves the scored test complete.\n   242\t  - Records are split on '\\n' only, the writer's delimiter. An answer may contain other Unicode line separators (U+2028, U+0085,\n   243\t    U+2029), and these are kept inside the record.\n   244\t  - Rehearsed: a torn retry record leaves the verdict complete; a torn scored record (the existing control) makes it INCOMPLETE; an\n   245\t    answer holding U+2028, U+0085 and U+2029 stays one record; the order of every first attempt before any retry is checked on the\n   246\t    provider's own call sequence.\n   247\t- **Rehearsal:** 63 of 63, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   248\t- **Mutants:** 33 of 33 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   249\t  - One mutant (splitting on any line break) is caught when a scenario guard stops the rehearsal: 36 attempts started, 35 finished.\n   250\t  - The mutant harness now counts such a stop as a catch and shows its reason.\n   251\t\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n   283\t\n   284\t## D753. The one-time v13s re-send (Alex: \"破例一次，付费重发\"), prepared before any answer exists\n   285\t\n   286\t- **The plan.** `paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned `0dc7c310…` in `paid-plan-v13s.sha256`. It holds 12 requests × 3 draws = 36 first\n   287\t  attempts. Every request's system text is the registered D751 request (`080a0012…`). The cases are unchanged: three pairs, then O,\n   288\t  S (CY2027) and E.\n   289\t- **The cap.** $0.50 in total, diagnostic retries included (D732 and D753).\n   290\t- **Authorization.** One-time, at `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/authorization.json`. The spent v13 authorization and the v13 pin\n   291\t  are unchanged. `send()` picks the pin and the authorization by the plan's format and refuses a mixed plan.\n   292\t- **Checked at $0,** with a stub gate and scratch key paths:\n   293\t  - an altered plan is refused, and so is a wrong ceiling;\n   294\t  - the pinned plan passes;\n   295\t  - a second use of the authorization is refused, and so is the spent v13 plan.\n   296\t- **Changes from council round 70** (`codex-r70.md`), made before the send. The verdict lines, the four questions and the\n   297\t  third-reader rule are unchanged.\n   298\t  1. **The card renderer** (`card_view`, `normalise`) now shows every figure and passage the card's prose names, with the figures\n   299\t     they rest on, and a written range such as e5399–e5404 in full. Figure ids inside the prose (reasons, why, basis_text) are\n   300\t     renumbered with the figures, so a prose reference points to the figure the writer meant.\n   301\t     - Checked at $0 on 20 stored v13s answers (D749–D751 and two controls): no dangling figure or passage reference, and every\n   302\t       shown value equal to the writer's.\n   303\t     - An unresolved card keeps the passages it weighed (8–9 each).\n   304\t  2. **The reader brief** is `reader-brief-v13s.md`. It is the v13 brief with Alex's two rulings, the same words for both readers and\n   305\t     the third reader:\n   306\t     - `usable` accepts an explained related figure (D747) and a \"can't tell yet\" that weighs the evidence, gives the target as\n   307\t       context and names the deciding fact (D753);\n   308\t     - `deciding_gap` is yes for a published number whose band an unsized adjustment determines, and no for a \"can't tell yet\".\n   309\t  3. **The exact file.** Readers receive the exact `packets.md` (`assemble_readings.py split-exact`; `third-exact` for the third\n   310\t     reader), with their packet ids named separately, so the sha256 the readings carry is the text they read.\n   311\t  4. **The launch.** It runs from the repository root, detached, with the log and pid outside the run folder:\n   312\t     `python3 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py send poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 0.5\n   313\t     docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.json`.\n   314\t     - All 36 scored attempts precede any diagnostic retry.\n   315\t     - A terminal transport failure on a first attempt makes the result INCOMPLETE.\n   316\t- **Re-checked after the changes:** rehearsal 19 of 19, paid mutants 33 of 33 with the control passing, cases 111 of 111, and the plan\n   317\t  pin unchanged.\n     1\t# Blind reading brief: judging-v13s paid gate (PAID-GATE.md §4, with Alex's rulings D747 and D753)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are a blind reader. The packets below each hold one or two cards. A card is a forecast answer to one question about a company\n     4\tfigure. For each card the packet shows:\n     5\t- the question and its ladder of rungs;\n     6\t- every passage the answer names, exactly as the model was shown it;\n     7\t- the figures the answer declared (a source figure read from a passage, a computed figure, or an estimate stated as the model's own);\n     8\t- the outcome as the code recomputed it from those figures;\n     9\t- the assumptions the code recorded (an overlap, an adjustment or a bridge, and whether it can move the outcome across a rung boundary);\n    10\t- the card itself (its rung, its reference, its reasons and its citations).\n    11\t\n    12\tA card with no answer says why in plain words.\n    13\t\n    14\tFor **every card**, answer the four questions below. Each answer is yes or no, with a ground. A ground is a short sentence that names\n    15\tat least one id from **the same packet**: a card (K1, K2), a passage (e123) or a figure (F4).\n    16\t\n    17\t1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on.\n    18\t   - A forecast may rest on a related figure when the passages do not give the asked quantity, if the card explains why the\n    19\t     comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under its own stated assumptions, its band is\n    20\t     more likely. The other band may remain possible.\n    21\t   - A card that answers \"can't tell yet\" (unresolved) is usable when it weighs the evidence, gives the company's target as context\n    22\t     where there is one, and names the fact that would decide the band. A bare statement of uncertainty is not usable.\n    23\t2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction. For a packet with one card, the\n    24\t   answer is no.\n    25\t3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation.\n    26\t4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n    27\t   - A published number that rests on an unsized adjustment (a share, deduction, discount or pace the passages neither size nor\n    28\t     bound) that determines its band: yes. A card that answers \"can't tell yet\" has no band: no.\n    29\t\n    30\tRules:\n    31\t- Judge only from the packet text: the passages, the figures and the card. Do not use outside knowledge of the company.\n    32\t- Read only the packet text given to you. Do not open any other file. Do not guess how a packet was produced.\n    33\t- A card that has no answer cannot be usable.\n    34\t\n    35\tReturn only JSON, in this shape (every packet and every card of your batch, all four questions each):\n    36\t\n    37\t```json\n    38\t{\"P01\": {\"K1\": {\"usable\": {\"answer\": \"yes\", \"ground\": \"...\"}, \"contradiction\": {\"answer\": \"no\", \"ground\": \"...\"},\n    39\t                \"internal_reference\": {\"answer\": \"no\", \"ground\": \"...\"}, \"deciding_gap\": {\"answer\": \"no\", \"ground\": \"...\"}},\n    40\t         \"K2\": {...}}}\n    41\t```\n--- reader-brief-v13.md\t2026-11-22 15:23:46\n+++ reader-brief-v13s.md\t2026-11-23 02:09:43\n@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@\n-# Blind reading brief: judging-v13 paid gate (registered in PAID-GATE.md §4)\n+# Blind reading brief: judging-v13s paid gate (PAID-GATE.md §4, with Alex's rulings D747 and D753)\n \n You are a blind reader. The packets below each hold one or two cards. A card is a forecast answer to one question about a company\n figure. For each card the packet shows:\n@@ -15,10 +15,17 @@\n at least one id from **the same packet**: a card (K1, K2), a passage (e123) or a figure (F4).\n \n 1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on.\n+   - A forecast may rest on a related figure when the passages do not give the asked quantity, if the card explains why the\n+     comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under its own stated assumptions, its band is\n+     more likely. The other band may remain possible.\n+   - A card that answers \"can't tell yet\" (unresolved) is usable when it weighs the evidence, gives the company's target as context\n+     where there is one, and names the fact that would decide the band. A bare statement of uncertainty is not usable.\n 2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction. For a packet with one card, the\n    answer is no.\n 3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation.\n 4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n+   - A published number that rests on an unsized adjustment (a share, deduction, discount or pace the passages neither size nor\n+     bound) that determines its band: yes. A card that answers \"can't tell yet\" has no band: no.\n \n Rules:\n - Judge only from the packet text: the passages, the figures and the card. Do not use outside knowledge of the company.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
