plan item) through `card_lines` in memory. Confirm the previously lost passages and figure references are now shown and\n    18\t     resolve, and that no value changed.\n    19\t2. **Does the new reader brief carry D747 and D753 faithfully,** with the four questions, the verdict lines and the third-reader rule\n    20\t   unchanged? Does it name no case?\n    21\t3. **Is anything left that would waste the send:** the plan pin, the cap, the authorization path, the launch command and the log\n    22\t   outside the run folder?\n    23\t4. **Verdict:** send, or do not send (with the blocking reason).\n    24\t\n    25\tReturn a short numbered report with citations, then the verdict.\nround70-brief.md:23:    detached, with a log and a pid file.\nPAID-GATE.md:311:  4. **The launch.** It runs from the repository root, detached, with the log and pid outside the run folder:\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:1095:  outcome of three passes), the judge and production (one day) each sent every network call under a ledger reservation; a ledger\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:1145:  network loss, each attempt on the ledger). The clean week draw completed from empty (`poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/`, $2.52; both ledgers $4.69). **Result (D489,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
