{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files --no-ignore poc/data /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind -g 'packets.md' 2>/dev/null | rg 'paid|v13-gate' | head -10\nnl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '425,440p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '647,669p'\nrg -n 'def run|reserve' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | tail -16\"","aggregated_output":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m19/work/abstain/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m19/work/separate-agree-float/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m19/work/clean/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m19/work/one-transport/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m19/work/retry/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m19/work/clean-changed/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m17/work/abstain/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m17/work/torn/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m17/work/separate-agree-float/packets.md\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-47d/m20/work/abstain/packets.md\n   425\t  shared modules.\n   426\t- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\n   427\t  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\n   428\t  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n   429\t- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\n   430\t  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\n   431\t- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.\n   432\t- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and\n   433\t  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.\n   434\t- Experiment harnesses send concurrently (a thread pool of 8; the archive is thread-safe); serial sends waste the wall clock Alex is\n   435\t  waiting on.\n   436\t- **Run settings** (`scripts/replay.py`): extraction requests prepared 16 at a time (`--workers`; the measurement launcher passes its\n   437\t  `HIVEMIND_WORKERS` there), Jev matching 8 at a time (`--jev-workers`), judgements 32 at a time (`judging.JUDGE_WORKERS`); a model call\n   438\t  times out after 180 s and is tried up to three times.\n   439\t  The three draws of a measurement run at once, one launcher each (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/run_arm.sh`). Measured\n   440\t  timings: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, \"Run settings and timing\".\n   647\t\n   648\t\n   649\tdef key_commitment(key):\n   650\t    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(key, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n   651\t\n   652\t\n   653\tdef render_packets(out, key):\n   654\t    \"\"\"The scoring packets for a key {salt, run_digest, order}: the key's salted sha256 first (so the text the readers receive commits\n   655\t    to the mapping), then each packet in the key's order, rendered from the run's results and plan.\"\"\"\n   656\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   657\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   658\t    units = packet_units(results, items)\n   659\t    lines, rendered = [f'Key commitment: {key_commitment(key)}', ''], {}\n   660\t    for pid, unit_key in key['order']:\n   661\t        decision, per_card = units[tuple(unit_key)]\n   662\t        body, grounds, members = packet_body(items, unit_key[0], unit_key[1], decision, per_card)\n   663\t        lines += [f'## {pid}'] + body\n   664\t        rendered[pid] = {'unit': unit_key[0], 'arm': unit_key[1], 'draw': unit_key[2], 'decision': decision, 'grounds': grounds,\n   665\t                         'cards': {f'K{n}': v for n, v in enumerate(members, 1)}}\n   666\t    return '\\n'.join(lines), rendered, units\n   667\t\n   668\t\n   669\tdef returned_text(raw):\n7:Reservation per attempt: a language-model request reserves (2 × its JSON bytes + 4,096) input tokens and its whole output cap\n8:(`max_completion_tokens`) at `model.PRICES`; a Jev request reserves (2 × its bytes + 4,096) input tokens at Jev's input rate, times\n128:        Path(path).write_text(json.dumps({'ceiling': ceiling, 'spent': 0.0, 'reserved': 0.0, 'overrun': False, 'refused': 0, 'attempts': 0,\n131:    def reserve(self, amount):\n133:            granted = not (state.get('stopped') or state['overrun'] or state['spent'] + state['reserved'] + amount > state['ceiling'])\n135:                state['reserved'] += amount\n153:    def settle(self, reserved, actual, kind='llm', tokens=None):\n159:            actual = reserved\n161:            state['reserved'] = max(0.0, state['reserved'] - reserved)\n163:            if actual > reserved + 1e-12:\n167:        self._note({'kind': kind, 'reserved': reserved, 'charged': actual, **({'tokens': tokens} if tokens is not None else {})})\n274:            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n295:        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
