{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'v13-paid|paid-v13|v13-paid-gate' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{PAID-GATE-RESULT.md,PAID-GATE.md,round70-brief.md} | head -28 && nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json | sed -n '80,101p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:63:  - `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json` is created exclusively at the first send, so a second launch is refused;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:255:  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:10:- **Run:** `poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`, sent once (D732) with gpt-6-luna. The ledger records 72 attempts and\n    80\t      \"rung\": null,\n    81\t      \"reference_unavailable\": null,\n    82\t      \"reasons\": \"NVIDIA's doubling outlook puts the reference at $40 billion, the lower edge of rung 2. Kress described growth as more than doubling, without sizing the excess. The FY2027 base is itself a target. Broad planned deployments and Anthropic's evaluation make an on-time ramp plausible. The stronger calendar 2027 hyperscaler spending outlook also gives those customers room to buy. Yet a major customer can deploy Vera in a small initial order or across many systems, with very different revenue in FY2028. AMD's agentic-workload tests give buyers a concrete reason to consider EPYC, but disclose no customer switching an order or negotiating a lower Vera price. Industry growth and Arm server adoption likewise give no Vera-specific order volume. Together these observations support demand and identify competitive risk, but do not favor either side of $40 billion.\",\n    83\t      \"why\": \"The decisive unknown is how many Vera CPUs customers will take during FY2028 and at what realized price. There is no booked volume, delivery schedule, or reported sales pace to size the gap between evaluations and revenue. Taking the target in full and discounting it into rung 3 would each require an unsupported assumption about that gap.\",\n    84\t      \"cites\": [\"e3660\", \"e4691\", \"e4856\", \"e4689\", \"e5044\", \"e5403\", \"e4687\", \"e4857\", \"e4692\"],\n    85\t      \"pushes\": [\n    86\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e3660\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    87\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4687\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    88\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4689\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    89\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4691\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n    90\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4692\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    91\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4764\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n    92\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4856\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n    93\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4857\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    94\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5044\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    95\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5399\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    96\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5400\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    97\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5401\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    98\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5402\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    99\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5403\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   100\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5404\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}\n   101\t      ],\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
