{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"ls poc/data | rg 'judging-v13|paid' | head -70 && head -40 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md && ls -d /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/*/scratchpad/paid-mutants-d753/m00/work/clean && nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '715,734p'\"","aggregated_output":"judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22\njudging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22.launch.log\njudging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22.launch.pid\njudging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22\njudging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22\njudging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22\njudging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23\njudging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23\njudging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23\njudging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23\n# judging-v13 paid gate: result (D733)\n\n**STOP.** Every one of the 72 answers was refused by the code checks: 36 scored first attempts and 36 diagnostic retries. Nothing\nwas published, and the joint arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs against the registered 8 of 9.\n\nThe result does not answer the question the gate was built for: does judging related number questions in one call give better\nnumbers than judging each alone? It shows that the answer format, as the request stated it, could not be filled. Most refusals are\nrules the request never stated, or checks that refuse right answers. A few are the model's own errors.\n\n- **Run:** `poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`, sent once (D732) with gpt-6-luna. The ledger records 72 attempts and\n  $0.3677 of the $0.50 ceiling: $0.1554 for the first attempts and $0.2124 for the retries. Every attempt finished with status\n  `answered`, so the result is complete, not INCOMPLETE.\n- **The blind reading** was not run. The registered brief says \"A card that has no answer cannot be usable\", and every card has\n  none, so the readers cannot change the verdict.\n- **Council round 48:**\n  - `round48-brief.md`;\n  - `claude-r48.md`, Claude's reflection, written first;\n  - `codex-r48.md`, an independent fresh read-only Codex session that reproduced every refusal from the journals and the requests.\n\n## 1. Census (first attempt → retry; Codex's count, which corrects Claude's)\n\n| Attempt | Arm | Answers | Structure (C7) messages / answers | Stopped at the structure check |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| First | Joint | 9 | 39 / 9 | 9 |\n| First | Separate | 18 | 47 / 18 | 17 |\n| First | Single | 9 | 13 / 9 | 8 |\n| Retry | Joint | 9 | 40 / 9 | 9 |\n| Retry | Separate | 18 | 41 / 18 | 14 |\n| Retry | Single | 9 | 12 / 9 | 6 |\n\n`check()` returns early after any structure error, so most source, arithmetic and compatibility checks never ran on these answers.\n\n**Prose where the check expects an id**, counted by occurrence:\n\n| Field | First | Retry |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `answers[].outcome` | 45 of 45 | 45 of 45 |\n| `answers[].reference.figure` | 39 | 32 |\n| `figures[].evidence` (139 of them on source figures, where C1 needs a passage id) | 175 | 133 (95) |\n| `figures[].bridge` | 49 | 44 |\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants-d753/m00/work/clean\n   715\t    rng = random.Random(secrets.randbits(64))\n   716\t    unit_keys = sorted(packet_units(results, items))\n   717\t    rng.shuffle(unit_keys)\n   718\t    earlier = sorted((k.split('|')[0], k.split('|')[1], k.split('|')[2], v, a['attempt'])     # every retry, and every format failure\n   719\t                     for k, e in results['finals'].items() for a in (e.get('attempts') or [])\n   720\t                     if a['attempt'] >= 2 or a.get('status') == 'format invalid'\n   721\t                     for v in items[tuple(k.split('|')[:2])]['members'])\n   722\t    rng.shuffle(earlier)\n   723\t    key = {'salt': secrets.token_hex(16), 'run_digest': run_digest(out), 'order': [(f'P{n:02d}', list(u)) for n, u in enumerate(unit_keys, 1)],\n   724\t           'attempts': [(f'D{n:02d}', list(e)) for n, e in enumerate(earlier, 1)]}\n   725\t    text = render_packets(out, key)[0]\n   726\t    attempts_text = render_attempts(out, key['attempts'])          # [47f.2] both rendered before anything is written\n   727\t    if (out / 'packets.md').exists() or (out / 'attempts.md').exists():\n   728\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} already holds packets; refused')\n   729\t    key_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   730\t    with open(key_dir / 'packet-key.json', 'x') as handle:\n   731\t        json.dump(key, handle, indent=1)\n   732\t    with open(out / 'packets.md', 'x') as handle:\n   733\t        handle.write(text)\n   734\t    with open(out / 'attempts.md', 'x') as handle:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && diff -u /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/*/scratchpad/s4treeA/assemble_readings.py assemble_readings.py | rg '\"'^@@|''^[-+]def'\"' && nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '254,275p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && diff -u /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/*/scratchpad/s4treeA/assemble_readings.py assemble_readings.py | rg '\"'^@@|''^[-+]def'\"' && nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '254,275p'\"","aggregated_output":"@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@\n@@ -44,6 +46,40 @@\n+def split_exact(packets_path, out, batches, brief_path):\n+def third_exact(packets_path, a_path, b_path, out, brief_path):\n@@ -90,6 +126,10 @@\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
